{
  "title": "Prayer for Fulfillment of Desires at Masjid al-Kufah",
  "data": "Offer a two-unit prayer in Masjid al-Kufah. In each unit, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5), [al-Falaq](A117), [al-Nas](A118), [al-Tawhid](A116), [al-Kafirun](A113), [al-Nasr](A114), [al-Qadr](A101) and [al-A'la](A91).\nAfter the prayer, recite the Tasbih al-Zahra' and ask Allah for your needs.\nThe Surahs may be recited in any order, as long as Surah al-Fatihah comes first.",
  "merits": "Imam al-Sadiq (‘a) is reported to have said that one who offers this prayer at Masjid al-Kufah will have all his requests settled.\n\nThis order of Surahs is corresponding with the order adopted by Sayyid Ibn Tawus in his book of al-Misbah, while according to the narration of Shaykh al-Tusi in his book of al-Amali, Surah al-Qadr follows Surah al-A’la. Possibly, the commitment to the order of the Surahs is not obligatory; therefore, it is acceptable to recite these seven Surahs in any order as long as Surah al-Fatihah precedes the others. Finally, Almighty Allah knows best."
}
